//
// ============================================================================
// EXTERNAL DEPENDENCIES NOT YET PORTED (throwing stubs, cited)
// ============================================================================
// The KEX rerelease folded the ROGUE mission-pack's "new AI" blocking/dodge/
// duck/jump-prediction system into the BASE game monster set (soldier,
// infantry, gunner, berserk, gladiator all call into it now -- confirmed by
// grepping every m_*.cpp in the source tree), but that whole file,
// rogue/g_rogue_newai.cpp, is out of this porting round's scope (this unit
// is five monster files + a test file only; no src/kexgame/g_rogue_newai.ts
// exists yet). Every symbol below is declared in g_local.h but DEFINED only
// in rogue/g_rogue_newai.cpp -- confirmed by grepping every .cpp in the
// rerelease tree for each definition. Local throwing stubs, matching
// m_gladiator.ts's own `blocked_checkplat` stub precedent exactly:
// - `blocked_checkplat` (rogue/g_rogue_newai.cpp:14) -- identical stub to
//   m_gladiator.ts's own copy.
// - `monster_jump_finished` (rogue/g_rogue_newai.cpp:101)
// - `blocked_checkjump` + `blocked_jump_result_t` enum (g_local.h:2546-2554,
//   rogue/g_rogue_newai.cpp:123)
// - `PredictAim` (rogue/g_rogue_newai.cpp:1083)
// - `M_MonsterDodge` (rogue/g_rogue_newai.cpp:1304, a MONSTERINFO_DODGE
//   handler -- signature matches `MonsterinfoDodgeFn` so `self.monsterinfo.
//   dodge = M_MonsterDodge` still type-checks, same treatment g_turret.ts
//   gives its own `infantry_pain`/`infantry_stand` stubs)
// - `monster_duck_down`/`monster_duck_hold` (rogue/g_rogue_newai.cpp:1424,
//   1434)
// - `monster_duck_up` (rogue/g_rogue_newai.cpp:1442, a MONSTERINFO_UNDUCK
//   handler -- signature matches `MonsterinfoUnduckFn`)
// `monster_done_dodge` is ALSO a throwing stub here, for the same reason
// g_ai.ts already carries its own non-exported local stub for it (pending
// rogue/g_rogue_monster.cpp:98, a DIFFERENT rogue file than the newai one
// above) -- g_ai.ts's copy is not exported, so it can't be imported; this
// file needs its own copy of the identical stub.
//
// ============================================================================
// PLACEMENT-MISMATCH FUNCTIONS PORTED LOCALLY -- see m_gladiator.ts header
// ============================================================================
// - `monster_footstep` (g_local.h:3282, `inline`) and `M_CheckGib`
//   (g_local.h:3521, `inline`) are trivial header-only helpers with no
//   rogue dependency -- reimplemented locally, exactly m_gladiator.ts's own
//   copies.
// - `giTraceline(start, end, passent, mask)` (g_local.h:136-139): the same
//   trivial `game_import_t::traceline` wrapper g_monster.ts's own local
//   (non-exported) copy documents; needed here by `berserk_attack_slam`.
//
// ============================================================================
// DEVIATIONS
// ============================================================================
// - `cached_soundindex` fields port as `{ index: 0 }` mutable boxes assigned
//   via a local `assignSound` helper -- m_gladiator.ts's own precedent.
// - `T_SlamRadiusDamage` (m_berserk.cpp:212-255): the C++ `point` parameter
//   is passed BY VALUE (`vec3_t point`, not `vec3_t &point`), so each call
//   gets one local copy that survives across the whole `while` loop --
//   `point[2] = ent->absmin[2]` on iteration N is NOT undone before
//   iteration N+1, so every subsequent entity's `v`/`dir` calculation in
//   the SAME call uses the PREVIOUS entity's absmin.z, not the original
//   impact point's z. Ported as one local mutable `point` copied once at
//   entry (`vec3(pointIn[0], pointIn[1], pointIn[2])`, matching this
//   codebase's established "Vec3 copy" idiom since a bare `=` would alias
//   the caller's array instead), then genuinely mutated in place across
//   loop iterations -- bug-for-bug, not a fresh copy per entity.
// - `blocked_jump_result_t` (g_local.h:2546-2551, `enum class`) is declared
//   locally as a plain object + type alias (this file's only consumer is
//   `berserk_jump`/`berserk_blocked`, both throwing-stub call sites today),
//   matching `GibTypeT`'s established object-enum idiom in this codebase
//   rather than a TS `enum`.
// - C++ `self->velocity = {}` (zero-init) -> `self.velocity = vec3(0, 0,
//   0)`, a genuinely fresh zeroed vector (not the shared `vec3_origin`
//   constant, which this codebase treats as a read-only default elsewhere).
// - Anonymous C++ lambdas inside `berserk_frames_run_attack1`'s thinkfunc
//   slots (m_berserk.cpp:425, 427, 428) become named local closures
//   (`berserk_run_attack1_frame1/3/4`) -- TS has no inline-lambda-as-table-
//   cell readability issue C++ doesn't already have, but named closures
//   keep this table's row count/structure diffable against the source.
// - `st.health_multiplier` -> `import { st } from "./g_spawn"` (the real,
//   shared spawn_temp_t global; g_spawn.ts already landed).
// - Frame index constants and `MODEL_SCALE` are local (non-exported) `const`s,
//   matching m_gladiator.ts's own precedent (not referenced elsewhere in
//   this porting batch, unlike m_player.ts/m_rider.ts's header-only ports).
//   Tests needing frame numbers read them off the exported `mmove_t`
//   objects' `firstframe`/`lastframe` fields instead.

